      ":question/id": "2b57157d-5ec3-5ac2-a4f8-1b8ad0001320",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n8\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right).\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{24}$ and then at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{12}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=4\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\\\\&=2\\,\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
